  <div style="padding-top:clamp(36px,5vw,68px)"><h1 class="dsub" style="font-size:clamp(38px,6vw,72px)">About</h1></div>
  <div class="aboutsplit">
    <div class="portrait"><img src="/img/mtl-1.jpg" alt="Ayush Prakash" /></div>
    <div class="prose">
    <p>Ayush Prakash studies how conversational AI systems are reshaping cognition, identity, agency, and human development in the first AI-native generation, and translates emerging research into public frameworks, policy ideas, and cultural understanding.</p>
    <p>He is Director of Corporate Strategy at <a href="https://newsapience.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--hair)">New Sapience</a>, a deterministic-AI company founded by veterans of DARPA, NASA, and the NSA, where he works on non-LLM machine cognition and leads business operations and institutional capital strategy.</p>
    <p>He is the author of AI for Gen Z, co-author of &ldquo;The Infinity of the Brain and the Void of the Machine&rdquo; with neuroscientist Karl Friston in The Montreal Review, and of &ldquo;The Risks of AI and Social Media for the Developing Brain&rdquo; with Dr. Ran Anbar in Psychology Today, and host of the Ayush Prakash Podcast: 150+ episodes with researchers and thinkers including Friston and Harvard astrophysicist Avi Loeb.</p>
    <p>His current project is The First AI-Native Generation, a living, source-linked analysis of the public podcast archive.</p>
    <p>Based in Montreal. English and French.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
